   },
   "source": [
    "**Your answer:** Explain the behaviour of the sample mean.\n",
    "\n",
    "The sample mean never converges to x0 = 20, even at N = 10^7. It keeps\n",
    "jumping and can swing far from the true value. \n",
    "\n",
    "This happens because the Cauchy distribution has no finite mean, so the law of large numbers\n",
    "does not apply. Therefore, increasing the sample size does not make the sample mean concentrate around $x_0$."
   ]
