   },
   "source": [
    "## Part 3 — Estimating both parameters\n",
    "\n",
    "### Provided example — Fit position and distance together\n",
    "\n",
    "Return to $x_0=20$ and $y_0=15$ for data generation, and now treat both parameters as unknown during fitting."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": [
     "provided"
    ]
   },
   "source": [
    "With independent uniform priors over sufficiently broad fixed intervals, the posterior is proportional to the likelihood within those intervals:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$p(x_0,y_0\\mid\\{x_k\\})\\propto p(\\{x_k\\}\\mid x_0,y_0).$$"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": [
     "provided"
    ]
   },
   "source": [
    "Generate $N=100$ flashes and plot the log-likelihood and relative likelihood as functions of both position and distance."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 53,
   "metadata": {
    "tags": [
     "provided"
    ]
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 720x480 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "x0_true = 20\n",
    "y0_true = 15\n",
    "N = 100\n",
    "tab_y0 = np.linspace(0, 2 * y0_true, 201)[1:]\n",
    "tab_x0 = np.linspace(x0_true - 2 * y0_true, x0_true + 2 * y0_true, 200)\n",
    "x = cauchy.rvs(loc=x0_true, scale=y0_true, size=N)\n",
    "\n",
    "X, Y = np.meshgrid(tab_x0, tab_y0)\n",
    "Z = np.array([[loglh(x0, y0, x) for x0 in tab_x0] for y0 in tab_y0])\n",
    "\n",
    "fig = plt.figure(figsize=(9, 6), dpi=80)\n",
    "ax = fig.add_subplot(111, projection='3d')\n",
    "ax.set_title('Log-likelihood', fontsize=16)\n",
    "ax.plot_surface(X, Y, Z, alpha=0.8)\n",
    "ax.plot([x0_true, x0_true], [y0_true, y0_true], [Z.min(), Z.max()], color='r')\n",
    "ax.set_xlabel(r'$x_0$', fontsize=14)\n",
    "ax.set_ylabel(r'$y_0$', fontsize=14)\n",
    "ax.set_zlabel(r'$L(x_0, y_0)$', fontsize=14)\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 54,
   "metadata": {
    "tags": [
     "provided"
    ]
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 960x800 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "relative_likelihood = np.exp(Z - Z.max())\n",
    "\n",
    "fig = plt.figure(figsize=(12, 10), dpi=80)\n",
    "ax = fig.add_subplot(111, projection='3d')\n",
    "ax.set_title('Relative likelihood', fontsize=16)\n",
    "ax.plot_surface(X, Y, relative_likelihood, alpha=0.8)\n",
    "ax.plot([x0_true, x0_true], [y0_true, y0_true], [0, 1], color='r')\n",
    "ax.set_xlabel(r'$x_0$', fontsize=14)\n",
    "ax.set_ylabel(r'$y_0$', fontsize=14)\n",
    "ax.set_zlabel(r'$e^{L-L_{\\max}}$', fontsize=14)\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": [
     "provided"
    ]
   },
   "source": [
    "Finally, fit both parameters for increasing sample sizes. As before, optimize the log-distance to keep the distance positive.\n",
    "\n",
    "Start with at least three flashes: one flash has no finite joint maximum-likelihood estimate, and two flashes do not give a unique one."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 55,
   "metadata": {
    "tags": [
     "provided"
    ]
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "CPU times: user 45.6 ms, sys: 3.2 ms, total: 48.8 ms\n",
      "Wall time: 49.3 ms\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "%%time\n",
    "\n",
    "def fit_parameters(x, func=loglh, x0_bounds=None, y0_max=None):\n",
    "    x0_guess = np.median(x)\n",
    "    if x0_bounds is None:\n",
    "        x0_bounds = (None, None)\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        x0_guess = np.clip(x0_guess, x0_bounds[0], x0_bounds[1])\n",
    "    y0_guess = np.median(np.abs(x - x0_guess))\n",
    "    if y0_max is not None:\n",
    "        y0_guess = min(y0_guess, y0_max)\n",
    "    log_y0_max = None if y0_max is None else np.log(y0_max)\n",
    "    if y0_guess <= 0:\n",
    "        raise ValueError('The observations must give a positive initial scale.')\n",
    "    params = checked_minimize(\n",
    "        lambda params: -func(params[0], np.exp(params[1]), x),\n",
    "        [x0_guess, np.log(y0_guess)],\n",
    "        bounds=[x0_bounds, (None, log_y0_max)],\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    return np.array([params[0], np.exp(params[1])])\n",
    "\n",
    "# Joint estimation uses N >= 3 to avoid the degenerate one- and two-sample cases.\n",
    "tab_N = np.unique(np.geomspace(3, 10_000, num=20).astype(int))\n",
    "x0_ML = []\n",
    "y0_ML = []\n",
    "for N in tab_N:\n",
    "    x = cauchy.rvs(loc=x0_true, scale=y0_true, size=N)\n",
    "    x0_estimate, y0_estimate = fit_parameters(x)\n",
    "    x0_ML.append(x0_estimate)\n",
    "    y0_ML.append(y0_estimate)"
   ]
